I've reviewed `src/pages/home/report/ReportActionCompose/ReportActionCompose.tsx`. This component is responsible for the composer, including the attachment picker. The key part is the `AttachmentModal` component on line 427:

```typescript
423                 <AttachmentModal
424                     headerTitle={translate('reportActionCompose.sendAttachment')}
425                     onConfirm={addAttachment}
426                     onModalShow={() => setIsAttachmentPreviewActive(true)}
427                     onModalHide={onAttachmentPreviewClose}
428                 >
429                     {({onConfirm}) => (
430                         <AttachmentPickerWithMenuItems
431                             onPress={onAddActionPressed}
432                             onItemSelected={onItemSelected}
433                             onTriggerAttachmentPicker={onTriggerAttachmentPicker}
434                             onCanceledAttachmentPicker={() => (isNextModalWillOpenRef.current = false)}
435                             onWillShowComposeMenu={() => (isKeyboardVisibleWhenShowingModalRef.current = false)}
436                             report={report}
437                             reportID={reportID}
438                             isMenuVisible={isMenuVisible}
439                             setMenuVisibility={setMenuVisibility}
440                             actionButtonRef={actionButtonRef}
441                             displayFileInModal={onConfirm}
442                             isBlockedFromConcierge={isBlockedFromConcierge}
443                         />
444                     )}
445                 </AttachmentModal>
```

This modal is used for the attachment *preview*, before the attachment is sent. Inside this modal, the `AttachmentView` component is used, but it's not wrapped in a `PressableWithoutFeedback` with a button role. This is why the cursor behaves correctly in the preview.

The problem lies in the attachment *viewer*, which is opened after the attachment is sent. This is handled by `AttachmentModal` as well, but in a different context. I will look at `src/components/AttachmentModal.tsx` to see how it handles the `onPress` prop.

